$DIR/main.p:8:2: cannot store c.Get in package variable F, which outlives main's frame
    A method value (at main.p:8) is a record in main's frame that holds its
    receiver, and calling it calls the method on that receiver. When main
    returns, its frame is reclaimed, but package variables live for the whole
    program, so package variable F would be left pointing at reclaimed memory.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Store the value itself instead of a view of main's frame, or allocate it so
    that it lives as long as package variable F.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3002" for a longer explanation)
